  "findings": [
    "The whole mean-IoU deficit sits in the low-observed-growth tercile (ratio <= 1.36): SimFire adds about 262 cells where FEDS adds about 59, with 2.9% precision; that tercile sums to -25.4 IoU against a cohort total of -22.8.",
    "In the high-growth tercile SimFire already beats persistence by +0.035 mean IoU (new-cell precision 0.48).",
    "Even at WAF 0.01, SimFire grows in 63% of timepoints, nearly independent of whether FEDS grows (82%); growth recall is 8.5%. The failure is weak discrimination of which fires grow, not wind direction.",
    "Many low-growth FEDS fires are likely contained or suppressed in reality; a free-burning no-op cannot represent that, so persistence is a structurally strong reference."
  ]
